    <dl>
      <dt>Resort type</dt><dd>Deluxe Villa resort at Disney's Contemporary Resort, in the Magic Kingdom Resort Area. Disney Vacation Club inventory is mixed with cash bookings.</dd>
      <dt>Address</dt><dd>4600 North World Drive, Lake Buena Vista, FL 32830 (same campus as the Contemporary; confirm check-in location on your reservation)</dd>
      <dt>Size</dt><dd>A high-rise tower next to the Contemporary, connected by a skybridge to the Main Tower monorail station and restaurants.</dd>
      <dt>Rooms</dt><dd>Deluxe Studios sleep 4; one-bedroom villas sleep 5; two-bedroom villas sleep 9; three-bedroom Grand Villas sleep 12. A single child under 3 in a crib does not count toward the maximum.</dd>
      <dt>Beds</dt><dd>Studio: 1 queen and 1 double-size pull-down. One-bedroom: 1 king, 1 queen-size pull-down and 1 single pull-down. Two-bedroom: 1 king, 2 queens, 1 queen-size pull-down and 1 single pull-down. Grand Villa: 1 king, 4 queens and 1 double-size pull-down.</dd>
      <dt>Getting around</dt><dd>Walking path to Magic Kingdom; monorail to Magic Kingdom, and to EPCOT via a transfer at the Transportation and Ticket Center, from the Contemporary. Boats also connect the Contemporary with Wilderness Lodge and Fort Wilderness. Buses to Hollywood Studios, Animal Kingdom, the water parks and Disney Springs</dd>
      <dt>Food</dt><dd>Shared with the Contemporary: Chef Mickey's, California Grill, Steakhouse 71 and Contempo Cafe</dd>
      <dt>Pools</dt><dd>Tower guests use the Contemporary Feature Pool (17-foot slide) and the quieter Bay Lake Pool. Whether the tower has a separate pool of its own is <span class="verify">[verify]</span>.</dd>
