  <section id="best-for">
    <h2>Who Bay Lake Tower is best for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Families who want a walk or a monorail to Magic Kingdom, plus a kitchen.</strong> The skybridge puts you in the Contemporary's Main Tower for the monorail and the restaurants.</li>
      <li><strong>Groups who will pay for a Theme Park View.</strong> Official listings include Magic Kingdom views on studios through Grand Villas, at a higher rack rate than Resort or Preferred (Bay Lake) views.</li>
      <li><strong>People who already like the Contemporary and need more than a hotel room.</strong> The hotel rooms, which often sleep five, have their own page.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Think twice if…</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You need a fifth bed in a studio.</strong> Official 2026 listings cap Deluxe Studios at four adults (a queen and a double-size pull-down). The Contemporary's standard hotel rooms are the ones that often sleep five.</li>
      <li><strong>A Resort View is just a polite name for parking.</strong> Official text describes some Resort Views as a parking area or an obstructed view. Read the category before you book.</li>
      <li><strong>You are sensitive to construction.</strong> A May 2026 planDisney answer described refurbishment work in the Contemporary atrium, on the Main Tower exterior and at Bay Lake Tower, expected to continue through late 2027. <span class="verify">[verify current status]</span></li>
    </ul>
